## THE STOP
The brief's clause: "If the census turns up a reader that can't repoint this
session, STOP -- Tony rules narrower-now vs. retirement-now with the census in
hand." Three did.

  testAction is parseAction's twin and inherits its open question verbatim --
  the brief already said of parseAction "it may need its own respelling rather
  than a repoint. If so, file, don't improvise." There are two of them.

  parseJSONarray and parseJSONfield are HAND-WRITTEN parse methods in
  RuleStuff.twk -- NOT emitter output, checked -- that fire the rule's action
  INLINE after a successful match. Under eviction they read a null gMethod:
  crash, or the action silently does not fire. Repointing them is not
  mechanical, because it decides whether a parse method fires the action inline
  or delegates to runRuleAction as the single door. That is Step E's invariant
  arriving early, inside Step C, on hand-written code.
